### Variables
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:5000
@nodeName = coinbase

### ============================================
### BASIC INFO ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### Get home/basic info
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### Get coinbase status
GET {{baseUrl}}/status

### Get coinbase balance
GET {{baseUrl}}/balance/coinbase

### Get all registered peers
GET {{baseUrl}}/peers

### Get full blockchain
GET {{baseUrl}}/chain

### Get mempool (pending transactions)
GET {{baseUrl}}/mempool

### ============================================
### TRANSACTION ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### Create transaction: coinbase → Alice (50 coins)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transaction/create?receiver=Alice&amount=50

### Create transaction: coinbase → Bob (30 coins)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transaction/create?receiver=Bob&amount=30

### Create transaction: coinbase → Charlie (20 coins)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transaction/create?receiver=Charlie&amount=20

### ============================================
### MINING ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### Mine a block (coinbase)
POST {{baseUrl}}/mine

### ============================================
### FAUCET ENDPOINT
### ============================================

### Request funds from faucet for Alice
POST {{baseUrl}}/faucet
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "node_name": "Alice"
}

### Request funds from faucet for Bob
POST {{baseUrl}}/faucet
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "node_name": "Bob"
}

### Request funds from faucet for Charlie
POST {{baseUrl}}/faucet
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "node_name": "Charlie"
}

### ============================================
### PEER REGISTRATION (used by other nodes)
### ============================================

### Register a new peer (example - normally done by other_node.py automatically)
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "TestNode",
  "port": 9000,
  "uuid": "test-uuid-12345",
  "host": "127.0.0.1"
}

### ============================================
### RECEIVE ENDPOINTS (used by network)
### ============================================

### Receive a transaction (example - normally done by other nodes)
POST {{baseUrl}}/receive_transaction
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sender": "Alice",
  "receiver": "Bob",
  "amount": 15,
  "timestamp": 1234567890.123
}

### Receive a block (example - normally done by other nodes)
POST {{baseUrl}}/receive_block
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "index": 5,
  "timestamp": 1234567890.123,
  "transactions": [
    {
      "sender": "Alice",
      "receiver": "Bob",
      "amount": 10,
      "timestamp": 1234567890.123
    }
  ],
  "previous_hash": "previous_hash_here",
  "nonce": 12345,
  "hash": "block_hash_here",
  "merkle_root": "merkle_root_here"
}

### ============================================
### WORKFLOW EXAMPLES
### ============================================

### WORKFLOW 1: Send funds to Alice and let her mine
# Step 1: Request faucet for Alice
POST {{baseUrl}}/faucet
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "node_name": "Alice"
}

###
# Step 2: Mine the block (do this on Alice's node at port 8001)
# See test_node.rest for Alice

### WORKFLOW 2: Coinbase sends money and mines
# Step 1: Create transaction
POST {{baseUrl}}/transaction/create?receiver=Bob&amount=25

###
# Step 2: Mine the block
POST {{baseUrl}}/mine

###
# Step 3: Check status
GET {{baseUrl}}/status

### ============================================
### DEBUGGING / MONITORING
### ============================================

### Check blockchain length
GET {{baseUrl}}/chain

### Check pending transactions
GET {{baseUrl}}/mempool

### Check all peer connections
GET {{baseUrl}}/peers

### Check specific node balance
GET {{baseUrl}}/balance/Alice

### Check another node balance
GET {{baseUrl}}/balance/Bob